cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "The multilinear gauge-invariant operator basis for five massless photons"
authors:
  - family-names: "Baca"
    given-names: "Martín"
repository-code: "https://github.com/martinbacaia/five-photon-operator-basis"
abstract: >
  Extends the S-matrix classification program of Henning-Lu-Melia-Murayama
  (arXiv:1706.08520) and Chowdhury-Gadde-Gopalka-Halder-Janagal-Minwalla
  (arXiv:1910.14392) to the spinning (photon) case at n=5 particles: S5
  representation theory on Mandelstam invariants, the complete invariant
  ring, photon polarization data structure, gauge-invariant building blocks
  (including a new "triple sandwich" atom), a parity theorem, and a
  classification through mass dimension 11.
keywords:
  - string theory
  - scattering amplitudes
  - S-matrix
  - representation theory
  - invariant theory
license: MIT
preferred-citation:
  type: generic
  title: "The multilinear gauge-invariant operator basis for five massless photons: representation theory, invariant ring, and a complete low-degree classification"
  authors:
    - family-names: "Baca"
      given-names: "Martín"
  year: 2026
  notes: "Preprint, not yet peer-reviewed. See paper/five-photon-operator-basis.pdf."
